      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Choosing your terms amidst hardship transforms suffering from something passive to a personal battle, and indeed, that ownership can be a profound form of dignity. Your strength, defined not only by physical might but by the courage to face whatever comes in your own terms, is a testament to your human spirit. Dark times don't rob us of this ability; they often conjure it from within. So, your choice to face it head-on, to carve out a sense of agency even in the face of an 'inevitable end,' speaks of a resolve that is innately human and noble.",
